-- title:
--   Definitions for Lagrangian representation for fermionic linear optics
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Lagrangian representation for fermionic linear optics* (arXiv:quant-ph/0404180) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `Grass`: PDF p.3: coefficients of ordered square-free Grassmann monomials.
--   - `grassOne`: PDF p.3: the scalar unit of the Grassmann algebra.
--   - `grassVar`: PDF p.3: variable with zero-based index a; zero outside the specified algebra.
--   - `grassMul`: PDF p.3, Eq.(6): exterior multiplication, with one minus sign per crossing. Intersecting supports contribute zero.
--   - `grassProd`: PDF p.3: ordered products; the empty product is the scalar unit.
--   - `grassPow`: PDF pp.3-4: powers used in the finite nilpotent Taylor series.
--   - `grassExp`: PDF p.4: finite exponential, used only on forms with zero constant term.
--   - `grassSubst`: PDF pp.3-4, Eqs.(9),(16): substitute linear Grassmann forms into a symbol.
--   - `blockVars`: PDF p.3: a consecutive variable block. All uses have block < blocks.
--   - `grassIntegrate`: PDF p.3: left Berezin integration of the variables after a retained prefix. The sign comes from moving the left derivatives past the retained monomial. Every application below integrates an even number of variables.
--   - `grassQuadratic`: PDF p.3: quadratic form without an implicit factor of one half.
--   - `basisOp`: PDF p.4: ordered Majorana basis element associated to a support.
--   - `majoranaSymbol`: PDF pp.2,4: the linear symbol map, via the trace-dual ordered CAR basis. It is not an algebra homomorphism.
--   - `StateWith`: PDF p.4, Definition 1: positive trace-one Gaussian density with real skew matrix and no linear Grassmann terms.
--   - `FermionicGaussianState`: PDF p.4, Definition 1, including mixed and rank-deficient densities.
--   - `regularCorrelation`: PDF pp.4-5: normalized complex correlation matrix of a regular operator. It is used only with nonzero trace; states have trace one.
--   - `RegularWith`: PDF p.5, Eq.(22): regular Gaussian operator with its complex skew matrix.
--   - `GaussianOperator`: PDF p.5, Definition 2: closure in the finite-dimensional operator topology of the nonzero-trace Gaussian operators. In particular zero is admitted.
--   - `InSector`: PDF pp.2,8: parity sector, defined on the full ordered CAR expansion.
--   - `ParityPreserving`: PDF p.8, Definition 4: both even and odd sectors are preserved.
--   - `ComplexLinear`: PDF p.7: complex linearity on every operator.
--   - `GrassmannKernel`: PDF p.7, Eq.(38): independent kernel parameters; Gaussianity alone imposes neither positivity nor trace preservation.
--   - `kernelAction`: PDF p.7, Eq.(38): action in arbitrary anticommuting variable blocks.
--   - `kernelEval`: PDF pp.7-8, Eq.(37): actual finite Berezin-kernel evaluation on any symbol. The variable order is theta, eta, mu; Deta Dmu integrates mu first.
--   - `HasGrassmannKernel`: PDF p.7, Definition 3: equality on all operators, including odd inputs.
--   - `GaussianMap`: PDF p.7, Definition 3, as an existential integral representation.
--   - `FullTracePreserving`: PDF p.9: TP is trace equality on all operators.
--   - `Bistochastic`: PDF p.9: bistochastic means TP and unital, without a CP requirement.
--   - `ordinaryExtension`: PDF p.9: ordinary extension E tensor Id, in first-factor block coordinates.
--   - `PositiveMap`: PDF p.9: positivity, without normalization or a trace bound.
--   - `LinearCompletelyPositive`: PDF p.9: complete positivity, tested on an equal-dimensional reference.
--   - `quadraticHamiltonian`: PDF p.2, Eq.(4): the source's quadratic Hamiltonian.
--   - `canonicalFLO`: PDF p.2: exactly exp(i H), with no additional scalar phase parameter.
--   - `IsCanonicalFLO`: PDF p.2: the canonical group generated by the stated real skew Hamiltonians.
--   - `Rotation`: PDF p.2: rotations are real special orthogonal matrices.
--   - `productState`: PDF p.4, Eq.(19): the full product density, including its normalization.
--   - `pfaffian`: PDF p.3: Pfaffian by the standard first-row pairing recursion. This reuses only the accepted algebraic recursion, not its Gaussian-state predicate.
--   - `modeProjector`: PDF pp.4,11: projector onto a specified occupation-number outcome. false denotes empty and true occupied.
--   - `firstK`: PDF pp.4-5,12: K supported only on the first mode, in zero-based indices.
--   - `lambdaOp`: PDF p.5, Eq.(24): Lambda in the ordinary two-copy algebra.
--   - `floMeasurementAction`: PDF p.11: projector action as a quadratic form on theta and eta. Its signs specify both outcomes and its missing two cross terms.
--   - `measurementEval`: PDF p.11, Eq.(51): finite evaluation of the measurement action.
--   - `homogeneousKernel`: PDF p.8: A=D=0 and arbitrary B, with prefactor one.
--   - `normalizeComplexTrace`: PDF pp.5,11: normalized state of a nonzero outcome; theorems guard its trace.
--   - `singularForm`: PDF p.5, Eq.(26): singular Gaussian symbol, with an even ordered prefix.
--   - `kernelBlock`: PDF p.9, Theorem 2: the complete skew block, with theta before eta.
--   - `RealContraction`: PDF p.9: entrywise reality and contraction in PSD matrix order.
--   - `ImplementsRotation`: PDF p.2, Eq.(5): the source's V c V-dagger convention.
--   - `firstEmbedding`: PDF pp.9-10, Eq.(48): first CAR-half embedding, with parity on the second ordinary tensor factor. This fixes the graded signs on odd operators.
--   - `doubleBasis`: PDF p.9: ordered basis of two disjoint CAR halves.
--   - `doubleCoefficient`: PDF pp.9-10: expansion coefficient in the full two-half CAR basis.
--   - `fermionicExtension`: PDF p.9, Definition 5: E tensor_f Id, extended linearly on every monomial. No equality with the ordinary extension is assumed.
--   - `dualReference`: PDF p.10, Definition 6: the fixed pure fermionic maximally entangled density.
--   - `fermionicDual`: PDF p.10: the unnormalized dual operator, for the fixed CAR identification.
--   - `doubleSymbol`: PDF p.10: theta then eta in a single anticommuting algebra; this is distinct from the ordinary tensor product of Grassmann algebras in Section V.
--   - `diagonalMap`: PDF pp.10-11: full diagonal map, specified on every ordered monomial.
--   - `elementaryMap`: PDF p.11: one elementary map rescales exactly the monomials containing a.
--   - `elementaryComposition`: PDF p.11: compose all elementary maps in increasing index order.
--   - `FLOProgram`: PDF pp.2,11-12: finite adaptive FLO program. At a measurement the two continuations may differ. A unitary input supplies its rotation exp(H), so the classical recurrence below uses only finite Grassmann arithmetic on given data.
--   - `RunTree`: PDF pp.1,12: a record at every stage and every outcome branch.
--   - `treeMap`: Apply a representation to every recorded state, preserving branch labels.
--   - `treeValues`: All records, including intermediate states and impossible branches.
--   - `treeLeaves`: Terminal records, ordered with the empty outcome before the occupied one.
--   - `quantumRun`: PDF pp.2,11-12: exact quantum semantics with unnormalized branch densities. Their traces are path probabilities, so zero branches require no normalization.
--   - `symbolicRun`: PDF pp.11-12: fixed finite classical recurrence of Gaussian integrals, computed from the initial covariance symbol. It never calls quantumRun.
--   - `operatorFromSymbol`: PDF pp.2,4: reconstruct an operator from its ordered CAR coefficients.
--   - `symbolCorrelation`: PDF p.4: recover the normalized complex covariance from a nonzero scalar symbol coefficient. Theorems use this only on positive-probability branches.
--   - `symbolWeight`: PDF p.12: path probability recovered from the constant Grassmann coefficient.
--   - `firstOutcomeSymbol`: PDF pp.11-12: the subnormalized empty-first-mode output symbol.
-- source:
--   Lagrangian representation for fermionic linear optics, arXiv:quant-ph/0404180v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0404180v2

import Mathlib
